WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.204 --> 00:00:24.117
"At least my laptop still works," Mr. Robbins said, even though he couldn't close his computer anymore because of the big dent from the crash.

2
00:00:24.118 --> 00:00:29.368
"I'm so sorry, Dad," Brooklyn said. "It was an accident."

3
00:00:29.369 --> 00:00:33.884
Her father nodded, but Brooklyn could tell he was still upset.

4
00:00:33.885 --> 00:00:42.606
"Dirk is right," Brooklyn thought. "I am a klutz—probably the clumsiest person in the whole world."

5
00:00:42.607 --> 00:00:48.773
At the next Whales practice, Brooklyn tried to keep her coaching tips for the players as quiet as possible.

6
00:00:48.774 --> 00:00:54.040
She made suggestions directly to Marv instead, and he took many of them.

7
00:00:54.041 --> 00:01:02.942
A few times Brooklyn noticed Jacey and other players rolling their eyes after Marv mentioned that Brooklyn had been the one to suggest something.

8
00:01:02.943 --> 00:01:05.912
Marv had noticed the players' responses too.

9
00:01:05.913 --> 00:01:12.666
"Coaches often have to put the team ahead of their own hurt feelings," he said quietly to Brooklyn.

10
00:01:12.667 --> 00:01:15.214
"You need thick skin to be a coach."

11
00:01:15.215 --> 00:01:18.356
Brooklyn knew the older coach was right.

12
00:01:18.357 --> 00:01:26.094
So at practice she started pretending there was dense fog in the gym and thick cotton in her ears.

13
00:01:26.095 --> 00:01:31.662
That way players' sour looks and unkind words couldn't reach her.

14
00:01:31.663 --> 00:01:39.162
Still, during the team warm-ups before Thursday's game, it was hard to ignore a player from the other team.

15
00:01:39.163 --> 00:01:45.742
She burst into laughter when Brooklyn stumbled over some practice balls.

16
00:01:45.743 --> 00:01:52.725
"Are you a player?" the tall girl from the Bobcats asked.

17
00:01:52.726 --> 00:02:00.217
"I'm the Whales' team manager." Brooklyn cleared her throat. "I'm also the assistant coach."

18
00:02:00.218 --> 00:02:08.391
"Assistant Coach Klutz!" The girl smirked and ran back onto the court to her teammates.

19
00:02:08.392 --> 00:02:12.173
Brooklyn shook her head and focused on her team's warm-ups.

20
00:02:12.174 --> 00:02:21.288
The ball bounced and flew from Jacey to Aaron to Stuart and around the whole roster of players.

21
00:02:21.289 --> 00:02:29.440
Suddenly Brooklyn realized a player was missing. She ran down the sideline to the gym office.

22
00:02:29.441 --> 00:02:38.177
She knocked and swung open the door. It banged into someone.

23
00:02:38.178 --> 00:02:41.834
"Ow!" It was the Bobcats' head coach.

24
00:02:41.835 --> 00:02:45.185
"Oops, sorry, sir!" Brooklyn said.

25
00:02:45.186 --> 00:02:51.350
The Bobcats' coach rubbed his arm. "I'm fine, I think."

26
00:02:51.351 --> 00:02:55.768
"Hi, Brooklyn. We're exchanging rosters for the game," Marv said.

27
00:02:55.769 --> 00:03:00.575
"Coach Teagan usually does this part. Are warm-ups going okay?"

28
00:03:00.576 --> 00:03:08.765
"Yep, but . . ." She wasn't sure if she should ask this question in front of the other coach. "Have you seen Dirk?"

29
00:03:08.766 --> 00:03:12.860
Marv's eyes widened. "He's not out there warming up?"

30
00:03:12.861 --> 00:03:15.248
Brooklyn shook her head.

31
00:03:15.249 --> 00:03:22.239
Marv and the Bobcats' coach looked at the clock over the desk. Dirk had about three minutes to arrive.

32
00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:26.412
Once the game began, no players could be added to the roster.

33
00:03:26.413 --> 00:03:30.538
"Dirk! You're here!" Jacey squealed from the court.

34
00:03:30.539 --> 00:03:34.897
"Never mind! Sounds like he's here," Brooklyn said.

35
00:03:34.898 --> 00:03:42.634
She walked back to the court, with the two men following.

36
00:03:42.635 --> 00:03:49.462
"I wonder if Marv will let Dirk play," she thought. "He missed all of warm-ups."

37
00:03:49.463 --> 00:03:57.769
Marv walked up to Dirk, who was tightening the laces on his sneakers. "You're late, Dirk."

38
00:03:57.770 --> 00:04:02.886
"I'm only here, Marv, because Coach Teagan said I should respect the team."

39
00:04:02.887 --> 00:04:10.282
He stood up. "I love the Whales, but I don't like that Brooklyn is trying to take over coaching."

40
00:04:10.283 --> 00:04:19.792
Brooklyn stepped closer. "I'm not trying to take over coaching, Dirk. I'm helping Marv. That's what Coach wanted me to do."

41
00:04:19.793 --> 00:04:28.936
Dirk didn't even look at her. "I'll play for you, Marv, but I won't do Brooklyn's goofy plays, including that girly loop play."

42
00:04:28.937 --> 00:04:31.682
Brooklyn pressed her lips together.

43
00:04:31.683 --> 00:04:36.660
Marv's voice was angry. "The Whales work and play together, Dirk.

44
00:04:36.661 --> 00:04:40.682
You're part of this team and that means doing what's asked of you.

45
00:04:40.683 --> 00:04:44.848
And remember, Brooklyn is part of this team too."

46
00:04:44.849 --> 00:04:47.255
Brooklyn just stood there.

47
00:04:47.256 --> 00:04:55.253
She wasn't sure whether to say something or just let Marv handle it. Didn't Dirk know that she loved the team too?

48
00:04:55.254 --> 00:05:02.060
The buzzer sounded. It was time to start the game.

49
00:05:02.061 --> 00:05:09.910
In the first quarter, Dirk barely moved around the court.

50
00:05:09.911 --> 00:05:15.242
Marv shouted at him. "Do you want the Whales to lose, Dirk?"

51
00:05:15.243 --> 00:05:20.636
It was clear to Brooklyn and everyone else that Dirk's heart wasn't in the game.

52
00:05:20.637 --> 00:05:25.301
At halftime Marv spoke to Dirk in a low, stern voice.

53
00:05:25.302 --> 00:05:30.876
"Make up your mind. If you want to be on this team, you have to play with the team.

54
00:05:30.877 --> 00:05:35.539
And don't forget that if we lose today, our season is over."

55
00:05:35.540 --> 00:05:42.453
Then Marv turned to the other players, trying to boost them with the team cheer. "Whales Whoosh!"

56
00:05:42.454 --> 00:05:48.453
Brooklyn kept her distance from Dirk, not bothering to speak to him or mention him to Marv.

57
00:05:48.454 --> 00:05:53.199
But a few seconds into the second half, she gasped.

58
00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:58.454
Dirk had just let a Bobcat player steal the ball!

59
00:05:58.455 --> 00:06:04.261
She leaned in to Marv and whispered, "Dirk might be trying to make us lose!"

60
00:06:04.262 --> 00:06:10.269
Marv clenched his jaw. "I hope you're wrong. I've got my eye on him."

61
00:06:10.270 --> 00:06:22.756
Then, in the final quarter, Dirk made a shot—one that flew through the Bobcats' net, giving the Bobcats the lead.

62
00:06:22.757 --> 00:06:29.479
Marv quickly called a time-out. "Stuart, you're in for Dirk."

63
00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:36.495
"What are you doing, Marv? Dirk's shot was an accident!" Jacey said. "We need Dirk!"

64
00:06:36.496 --> 00:06:40.715
"I forgot that we switched nets at the half," Dirk mumbled.

65
00:06:40.716 --> 00:06:42.819
Marv pointed to the bench.

66
00:06:42.820 --> 00:06:48.015
Dirk dropped down and draped a towel over his head.

67
00:06:48.016 --> 00:06:51.486
Brooklyn cheered on the team with Marv.

68
00:06:51.487 --> 00:07:01.138
In the final seconds, Stuart made a shot that put the Whales one point ahead of the Bobcats.

69
00:07:01.139 --> 00:07:05.722
She glanced over to see Dirk peeking out from under his towel.

70
00:07:05.723 --> 00:07:17.712
Maybe he didn't want to do Brooklyn's plays, but he looked happy when the final buzzer sounded and his team won by one point.

71
00:07:17.713 --> 00:07:25.704
After the game Brooklyn gathered up equipment. She saw Marv and Dirk talking in the office.

72
00:07:25.705 --> 00:07:32.943
When they came out, Marv gave everyone a quick talk about teamwork and getting ready to face the Terriers again.

73
00:07:32.944 --> 00:07:40.045
Then the players started packing up and leaving.

74
00:07:40.046 --> 00:07:47.576
Marv went back to the office. The only students left in the gym were Dirk, Stuart, and Brooklyn.

75
00:07:47.577 --> 00:07:50.850
"Great job today, Stuart," Brooklyn said.

76
00:07:50.851 --> 00:07:56.014
"You too, Coach Brooklyn," Stuart said, smiling and waving good-bye.

77
00:07:56.015 --> 00:08:01.171
"Hey, Dirk," she called. He didn't look up, so Brooklyn spoke louder.

78
00:08:01.172 --> 00:08:05.348
"It's okay if you're mad at me, but don't take it out on the team.

79
00:08:05.349 --> 00:08:08.749
The Whales need you to become league champions."

80
00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:17.401
Dirk kept moving to the exit, ignoring her. But Brooklyn knew he'd heard her.

81
00:08:17.402 --> 00:08:34.508
Brooklyn found her bag and then searched for her phone. She had one new text: Girls can't coach. Especially oafs like u.
